{"term":"foremost","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3133b1dd5b584e90cd","definition":"Positioned in front of (all) others in space, most forward.","example":"She prankes not by hir mistresse side, she preases not to bée / The foremost of the companie, as when she erst was frée.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["front","frontmost","forwardmost"],"antonyms":["back","backmost","hindmost","rear","rearmost","rearwardmost"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:63ebc711aae8e0859e","definition":"Coming before (all) others in time.","example":"[…] of both them, she / (By Pallas counsell) was to haue the grace / Of foremost greeting.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["first"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebc7ac03ad53e11b57","definition":"Of the highest rank or position; of the greatest importance; of the highest priority.","example":"The exhibition features works by the country’s foremost artists.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["greatest","leading","paramount","primary","principal","top"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:97a02288871d913c2a","definition":"Closest to the bow.","example":"I let fall the tiller, turned my back on them, and sat down on the foremost thwart.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["aftermost"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e387c708bc7e173c79","definition":"In front, prominently forward.","example":"No Man hath more nicely observed our Climate, than the Bookseller who bought the Copy of this Work; He knows to a Tittle what Subjects will best go off in a dry Year, and which it is proper to expose foremost, when the Weather-glass is fallen to much Rain.","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost","first and foremost","put one's best foot foremost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2e4cbe44efa4362b9c","definition":"First in time.","example":"c. 1618, Philip Massinger, Thomas Middleton and William Rowley, The Old Law, London: Edward Archer, 1656, Act III, Scene 1, p. 41,\nAlwayes the worst goes foremost, so twill prove I hope","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost","first and foremost","put one's best foot foremost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a3373f1e1b9c5e8156","definition":"Most importantly.","example":"[…] Mrs. Nickleby, with the utmost sincerity, gave vent to her sorrows after her own peculiar fashion of considering herself foremost,","pos":"adv","synonyms":["especially","particularly"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost","first and foremost","put one's best foot foremost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f5297901456ccccc5","definition":"A village in Alberta, Canada.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost","first and foremost","put one's best foot foremost"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Foremost#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈfɔː.məʊst/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/99/En-us-foremost.ogg/En-us-foremost.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["foremostly","headforemost","sternforemost","first and foremost","put one's best foot foremost"]}